abstract: >-
  We prove that the random Littlewood polynomials
  f_n(z) = ε_0 + ε_1 z + ... + ε_n z^n, built from one sequence of independent
  random signs, almost surely have n/2 + o(n) zeros in the closed unit disk,
  which resolves Erdős Problem #522. We prove an almost-sure radial law for the
  zeros at the scale 1/n around the unit circle, the same laws for Steinhaus,
  standard real and complex Gaussian, and nondegenerate bounded centrally symmetric
  coefficients, and the almost-sure bound n/2 + O(n/log n) for random signs.
  All main results have been formally verified in Lean 4 with Mathlib.
keywords:
  - random polynomials
  - Littlewood polynomials
  - zeros of random polynomials
  - almost sure convergence
  - Erdős problems
  - formal verification
